        <body>
            <div xml:id="d69">

                <pb facs="0199" n="95" sameAs="frus:frus1933v02/pg95"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.42157 Detroit/41</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Canada (Boal) to the Acting Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 57</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ottawa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-06-12">June 12,
                        1933</date>.<lb/>[Received June 14.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to my despatch
                    No. 1297 of March 23, 1933, and other correspondence with regard to operations
                    to be conducted in Canadian waters in connection with the dredging of certain
                    shoal areas in the St. Clair River, and to report the receipt of a note No. 68
                    of June 10, 1933, from the Department of External Affairs which modifies to some
                    extent the conditions imposed by the Canadian Government in its note No. 27 of
                    March 21, 1933, which was transmitted with the despatch under reference.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Pierre de L. Boal</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d69-a1.xml" xpointer="d69-a1"/>
            </div>
